1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,040
We'll speak a little bit about removal from

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:04,820
office of directors, because it's a strict provision

3
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:07,000
of the CARMA 2020.

4
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:10,080
If a director is to be removed from

5
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:13,260
office, whether it's executive or non-executive, there's

6
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:15,280
a requirement that he or she is given

7
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:18,800
28 days notice of the intention to remove

8
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:19,040
them.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,240
Within these 28 days, they have a right

10
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:26,400
to respond to the allegations made against them

11
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,080
or the reasons for which they're going to

12
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:28,600
be removed.

13
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:32,480
If it's a public company, the reasons have

14
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:35,240
to be published alongside the notice and the

15
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:38,420
response of the director to such allegations or

16
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:40,820
reasons would also be published as well.

17
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:43,680
And so to that extent, a lot of

18
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,940
companies would prefer that the director to be

19
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:49,960
removed is actually given the opportunity to resign.

20
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:53,440
And more so now that the requirement that

21
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:55,880
once the director is removed from office, he

22
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:57,600
or she can no longer hold the office

23
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:00,580
of a director, has caused many companies to

24
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:02,420
rethink the issue of removal.

25
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:06,040
It's a very extreme decision and extreme position

26
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:07,740
and so it's better to go the route

27
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:12,800
of having the director resign their role as

28
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:13,380
a director.

29
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:16,700
The board could potentially feel a casual vacancy

30
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:20,040
created by the exit of a director.

31
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:23,120
However, that casual vacancy has to be approved

32
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:26,400
by shareholders in the general meeting.
